+## Result Persistence Profile (`derived_pure_replay.v1`)
+
+`state.json` may carry one optional top-level selector, `result_persistence_profile`
+(additive; `schema_version` stays `2.1`).
+
+- Allowed values: absent (historical, bundle-backed persistence) or exactly
+  `derived_pure_replay.v1`. `to_dict()` omits the key when absent; a payload without it
+  loads as `None` and round-trips unchanged. Any other value fails closed with a
+  `ValueError` naming `result_persistence_profile` at `RunState` construction, at
+  `StateManager.initialize(...)`, and on load; a failed load never rewrites the file.
+  `initialize(..., result_persistence_profile=...)` writes the field in the first atomic
+  write, before any visit. Loading never infers, backfills or upgrades the field.
+- Selection: a successfully compiled typed public `.orc` run, a new root created by
+  `resume --force-restart` of an `.orc`, and a fresh non-iterative call frame whose callee
+  bundle has `provenance.frontend_kind == "workflow_lisp"` select the profile. Selection
+  never reads the parent's profile, a path suffix, an alias or a step identity. A fresh
+  retry after a failed non-iterative Workflow Lisp predecessor is new state and selects it.
+  Existing roots and frames, non-Workflow-Lisp callees and iteration-owned frames keep the
+  historical profile; an existing frame is never backfilled, and a malformed existing
+  frame (no mapping `state`) is rejected with `existing call-frame state ...` before any
+  write.
+- Eligible nodes: compiler-generated `pure_projection` nodes that are acyclic and visited at
+  most once per scope. Recurrent, loop-owned and otherwise multiply visited nodes
+  (`multiple_visit_region`) keep full rows, bundles and checkpoints. An imported callee is
+  indexed alone, under its own `root` scope.
+- Persisted shape: a successful eligible pure step stores exactly
+  `{"name", "step_id", "visit_count": 1, "status": "completed", "exit_code": 0,
+  "outcome": {"status": "completed", "phase": "execution", "class": "completed",
+  "retryable": false}, "result_storage": "derived_pure_replay.v1"}` and nothing else.
+  Failed and skipped rows stay full. No result bundle, `private_artifact_versions` entry,
+  checkpoint record or restore binding exists for an eligible node.
+- Progress: visit, cursor and row classify as `unstarted`, `interrupted`, `derived_complete`
+  or `durable_failure_skip`; every other combination (including any visit other than one) is
+  `progress_witness_invalid`.
+- Resume: required pure values are re-derived in memory from durable inputs (bound inputs and
+  durable step results) without dispatching effects, incrementing visits, settling results or
+  writing state. A run that cannot do so fails before any effect with
+  `error.type == "pure_result_replay_unavailable"` and `error.context.reason` one of
+  `durable_input_missing`, `durable_input_invalid`, `binding_unresolved`,
+  `evaluation_failed`, `output_contract_invalid`, `progress_witness_invalid`,
+  `profile_conflict` (with `context.surface` `steps`, `pure_bundle`,
+  `private_artifact_versions`, `checkpoint_record` or `restore_payload`),
+  `dependency_index_invalid`, `reachability_ambiguous` or `multiple_visit_region`.
+- Default resume admits one zero-record case, `VALIDATED_FRAME_ENTRY_REPLAY`
+  (`selection_reason: validated_frame_entry_replay`, no checkpoint id), only with validated
+  bound-input leaves and exact profile and progress witnesses; otherwise it fails closed with
+  `lexical_default_resume_prior_boundary_not_restorable`.
+
 ## State File Schema (example)
 
 The state file (`${RUN_ROOT}/state.json`) is the authoritative record of execution:
